How to Install Oracle Database 19c on Windows 10/11
Step 1: Download Oracle 19c
1.	Go to Oracle Official Website: https://www.oracle.com/database/technologies/
2.	Select Oracle Database 19c for Windows x64
3.	Login with your Oracle account (or create one if needed)
4.	Download the ZIP file (e.g., WINDOWS.X64_193000_db_home.zip)
Step 2: Extract the Installation Files
1.	Create a folder on your system, for example: C:\Oracle19c
2.	 Extract the downloaded ZIP file into this folder
3.	Make sure the folder path does not contain spaces
Step 3: Create Software Directory Structure
1.	Inside C:\Oracle19c, create a new folder named: app
Step 4: Run the Setup File
2.	Open the extracted folder
3.	Right-click on setup.exe
4.	Select Run as Administrator
Step 5: Installation Configuration
1.	Select Create and configure a single instance database
2.	Choose Desktop Class
3.	Select Use Windows Built-in Account
4.	For Oracle Base, click Browse and select: C:\Oracle19c\app
5.	Enter Global Database Name: orcl
6.	Enter Password (example: s)
7.	Confirm Password
8.	Keep Create as Container Database checked
9.	Enter Pluggable Database Name: orclpdb
10.	Click Next
11.	Click Install
12.	If prompted, allow access for Public Network
13.	Click Done after installation completes
✅ Installation Complete
Oracle Database 19c is now successfully installed on your Windows system.

